{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.PhotonIRZeroMode","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.PhotonIRZeroMode","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Pow.Real","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":15,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.PhotonIRZeroMode.photon_selfEnergy_betti_product","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.PhotonIRZeroMode.photon_selfEnergy_betti_product","kind":"theorem","line":144,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/PhotonIRZeroMode.lean#L144-L156","doc":"**n=1 ↔ n=2 unification on the genus-4 Hodge data.** Both IR corrections are\nbuilt from the single Betti number `b₁(M_g) = 2g`: the n=1 zero-mode carries\nit in the numerator (`photonZeroModeShift = b₁/Area`), the n=2 self-energy in\nthe denominator (`selfEnergyDenominator = π·b₁`). Their product is `π`-free,\n`b₁²/(4(g-1))` — the archimedean `π` cancels, leaving a topological ratio. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.PhotonIRZeroMode.selfEnergyDenominator_count_is_real","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.PhotonIRZeroMode.selfEnergyDenominator_count_is_real","kind":"theorem","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/PhotonIRZeroMode.lean#L128-L142","doc":"**The self-energy count is the REAL harmonic-1-form count, not the\nholomorphic one.** The photon is a real `U(1)` gauge field; its connection\nis a real 1-form, so the self-energy propagator lives on the kernel of the\n*real* Hodge Laplacian `Δ₁` on `Ω¹(M,ℝ)` — whose ζ-regularized index is\n`−ζ_{Δ₁}(0) = b₁ = 2g` (the merged area-free count, PR #3834/#3896), NOT the\n∂̄-Laplacian's holomorphic `g`. Hence at `g = 4` the denominator is\n`π·b₁ = π·(2·g) = 8π = 2·(4π)`, with the `2` FORCED to be the real-vs-complex\ndoubling. (This settles the *count*; the reciprocal normalization *form*\n— `π·b₁` vs the heat-kernel `(4π)·2` — is a separate, still-open question,\ntracked in the α_EM ledger and `alpha_em_multiplicity2_realcomplex_probe.py`.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.PhotonIRZeroMode.betti1_eq_two_holomorphic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.PhotonIRZeroMode.betti1_eq_two_holomorphic","kind":"theorem","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/PhotonIRZeroMode.lean#L120-L126","doc":"**Real-vs-complex Hodge doubling.** The real harmonic-1-form count is twice\nthe holomorphic count: `b₁ = 2·g`. This is the archimedean shadow of the\nHodge decomposition `H¹(M,ℝ) ⊗ ℂ = H^{1,0} ⊕ H^{0,1}`, each summand of\ncomplex dimension `g`. It pins WHERE the `2` in `8π = 2·(4π)` lives: it is\nthe real⊕complex doubling, not a free multiplicity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.PhotonIRZeroMode.holomorphicOneFormCount","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.PhotonIRZeroMode.holomorphicOneFormCount","kind":"def","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/PhotonIRZeroMode.lean#L114-L118","doc":"Holomorphic 1-form count `dim_ℂ H^{1,0}(M_g) = g` — the genus, i.e. the\nnumber of independent *holomorphic* differentials on a compact genus-`g`\nRiemann surface. Contrast `betti1 g = 2g`, the count of *real* harmonic\n1-forms `dim_ℝ H¹(M,ℝ)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.PhotonIRZeroMode.selfEnergyDenominator_at_g4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.PhotonIRZeroMode.selfEnergyDenominator_at_g4","kind":"theorem","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/PhotonIRZeroMode.lean#L106-L112","doc":"At `g = 4` the self-energy denominator is `8π` (since `b₁ = 2g = 8`),\nthus the n=2 term's `8π` is `π·dim H¹(M_Bring)` — the same Betti number that\ngives the n=1 zero-mode `2/(3π) = b₁/Area`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.PhotonIRZeroMode.selfEnergyDenominator","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.PhotonIRZeroMode.selfEnergyDenominator","kind":"def","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/PhotonIRZeroMode.lean#L96-L104","doc":"The **n=2 self-energy denominator** is `π · b₁(M_g)` — the *same* harmonic\n1-form count `b₁ = 2g` as the n=1 zero-mode, now in the denominator. This\ngrounds the empirical n=2 form `α·[2]_q/(8π)·(1−h²α)` of the α/(4π) thread\n(PR #1495 RT-plan Identity 1: `[2]_q/(8π) = [2]_q/(π·dim H¹(M_Bring))`).\n\nBoundary discipline: `b₁` is topological (`ℕ`), `π` is archimedean (`ℝ`);\nthe `[2]_q` numerator is the substrate Hecke integer, `τ_arch`-evaluated\nseparately (it is *not* an object of this archimedean computation). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.PhotonIRZeroMode.surface_minus_naive_g4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.PhotonIRZeroMode.surface_minus_naive_g4","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/PhotonIRZeroMode.lean#L83-L94","doc":"The difference surface-minus-naive at `g=4` has the closed form\n`(16π-9)/(24π²)` — positive for `π > 9/16` (the surface value\ndominates the naive `M×S¹` value). Pure algebra, no `π`-bound needed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.PhotonIRZeroMode.naiveCrossS1Shift","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.PhotonIRZeroMode.naiveCrossS1Shift","kind":"def","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/PhotonIRZeroMode.lean#L74-L81","doc":"The naive `M × S¹` shift: `b₁(M×S¹) = 2g+1` over `Vol = Area·2π = 8π²(g-1)`.\nAt `g = 4` this is `9/(24π²) ≈ 0.038`, strictly below the surface value\n`2/(3π) ≈ 0.212` — the recorded failed attempt. The strict inequality\nreduces to `π > 9/16` (true), and is witnessed numerically in\n`photon-ir-zero-mode-bring.witness.json` (the π-lower-bound import is\noutside this file's dependency cone). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.PhotonIRZeroMode.photonZeroModeShift_at_g4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.PhotonIRZeroMode.photonZeroModeShift_at_g4","kind":"theorem","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/PhotonIRZeroMode.lean#L65-L72","doc":"At `g = 4` (Bring's surface, `χ = -6`) the shift is `2/(3π)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.PhotonIRZeroMode.photonZeroModeShift_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.PhotonIRZeroMode.photonZeroModeShift_eq","kind":"theorem","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/PhotonIRZeroMode.lean#L57-L63","doc":"**From-the-Lagrangian core.** The photon IR zero-mode shift on the\ngenus-`g` surface is `2g/(4π(g-1))`. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:photon-ir-zero-mode-bring","label":"prop:photon-ir-zero-mode-bring","md":"quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/photon-ir-zero-mode-bring.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.PhotonIRZeroMode.area_eq_neg_two_pi_chi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.PhotonIRZeroMode.area_eq_neg_two_pi_chi","kind":"theorem","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/PhotonIRZeroMode.lean#L50-L55","doc":"**Gauss–Bonnet**: `Area = -2π·χ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.PhotonIRZeroMode.photonZeroModeShift","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.PhotonIRZeroMode.photonZeroModeShift","kind":"def","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/PhotonIRZeroMode.lean#L47-L48","doc":"Photon IR zero-mode shift `= (harmonic 1-form count) / Area = b₁/Area`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.PhotonIRZeroMode.area","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.PhotonIRZeroMode.area","kind":"def","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/PhotonIRZeroMode.lean#L43-L45","doc":"Hyperbolic area of a genus-`g` (`g ≥ 2`) surface at curvature `-1`, via\nGauss–Bonnet: `Area = -2π·χ = 4π(g-1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.PhotonIRZeroMode.betti1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.PhotonIRZeroMode.betti1","kind":"def","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/PhotonIRZeroMode.lean#L40-L41","doc":"First Betti number `b₁ = 2g` (rank of `H¹`, = harmonic 1-form count). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.PhotonIRZeroMode.eulerChar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.PhotonIRZeroMode.eulerChar","kind":"def","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/PhotonIRZeroMode.lean#L37-L38","doc":"Euler characteristic of a closed orientable genus-`g` surface, `χ = 2 - 2g`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}